    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d235">

                <pb facs="0340" n="328" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg328"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/5735</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">De la Casa</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]<anchor n="7" xml:id="d235-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 135/03</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-14">June 14, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to
                    Your Excellency the following information which I have received from my
                    Government.</p>
                <pb facs="0341" n="329" xml:id="pg329"/>
                <p>During the last few days more than one hundred German planes in the service of
                    the rebels have dropped tons of shrapnel (<hi rendition="#italic">metralla</hi>)
                    on the Basque people, bombing the fronts and the villages of that country and
                    continuing the terroristic methods which this same air force used in Durango and
                    Guernica. They threw more than fifty bombs on the Bilbao cemetery, destroying
                    hundreds of graves, scattering the remains of the dead, and causing a horrible
                    spectacle. The Government forces succeeded in bringing down three planes; one
                    [a?] Heinkel bimotor, Model 111, which fell within their lines, causing the
                    death of the crew, who were Germans, as in the case of all the other aviators
                    previously captured on this front.</p>
                <p>In compliance with the instructions of my Government, I advise Your Excellency of
                    the facts above stated and also place on record the protest of my Government
                    against the criminal action of the German air force assigned to service with the
                    rebels.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Enrique Carlos De La
                    Casa</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
